ar i found him to  be a lot more sympathetic of the  character still kind of a dickling but  better the second time around for sure  out of all the ha monkey lie envy hates  humans the most seeming to take the most  pride out of torturing them and making  them suffer the only one who this is  even comparable with is maybe pride  which to be fair they're both kind of  horrific monsters we see envy taking  pride in the fact that he played a role  in the incident which started the ishval  in war as well as just in general for  ruining the lives of countless people  all of this though stems from what his  name suggests envy specifically for  humanity's ability to endure as well as  for their knack to form close bonds  which cause them to love and support one  another as a homunculus he never really  experienced that and as such he aims to  destroy it when he sees it in others i  know i typically talk about appearance  first but with envy we kind of have to  talk about his ability because it's tied  to his appearance envy is a shapeshifter  being able to turn into anything or  anyone as long as it doesn't exceed the  mass of his true form and this true form  is kind of massive so it's usually not  an issue he can also change individual  parts of his body into things like  snakes or even giant portions of his  true form at will so it doesn't have to  be a 100 transformation kind of thing  along with this he can also imitate  people's personalities and voices but it  isn't a perfect impersonation his  overconfidence tends to shine through  and those who know the person he's  trying to imitate very intimately can  usually see through the disguise now on  to envy's true form this comes in two  parts firstly in a massive green lizard  monster with a dog's face long black  hair multiple eyes and a back that is  covered in the faces of humans who  represent those who died in xerxes it is  absolute nightmare fuel and of the  entire series it's probably one of the  images that stayed in my head the  longest after first watching it however  after most of his philosopher's stone is  destroyed he becomes a small green  parasite that can attach to people or to  mannequin homunculi and can even control  them if he bites into them of course he  eventually dies in this smaller form  choosing to take his own life when  edward explains that the homunculus is  in fact jealous of humanity's friendship  a reality that envy has been avoiding  his entire life and when faced with it  directly is something which led to him  removing his own philosopher's stone  full metal alchemist  our fourth homunculus is greed greed is  a surprisingly wise homunculus who is as  you might assume very very greedy his  worldview is one that suggests everyone  in the world is greedy while he himself  wants money women's status fame and  everything else the world has to offer  including eternal life he also argues  that everyone wants something and even  the desire to do good is a form of greed  greed is beyond charismatic and charming  and yes super narcissistic but in most  cases if he's not trying to take  something he's pretty easy going and  comfortable something which might stem  from his unique ability the ultimate  shield greed is able to harden the  carbon all over his body to make a dense  black material that coats his entire  body that is as durable as diamond he  can also cover specific points of his  body or inside his body as well and it  makes him essentially impervious to  damage with one of the only real  weaknesses being transmuting that carbon  to something less durable like when ed  changed it to graphite now combine this  ultimate shield with the general  homunculus trait of regeneration and  immortality and you get someone who is  extremely difficult to kill speaking of  difficult to kill he was killed ish by  father when his greed and goals were  revealed father elected to have him  drowned in molten gold which i mean gold  and greed is a pretty easy p