a little bit difficult to  describe everything that he's able to do  as just there's too much just know he's  basically all-powerful and able to do  whatever he wants in his prime but that  wraps up the brotherhood homunculus so  next let's take a look at their 2003  counterparts hot take by the way i think  the monkey light in 2003 are infinitely  more interesting i think that their  method of creation is so much more  poetically powerful and it adds a lot to  the story which just is lost in  brotherhood canon or not that's just my  opinion obviously there are some  elements from brotherhood that i think  far outweigh the 2003 version but when  it comes to homunculus as a group i  think 2003 has a little bit of an edge  so homunculus in the 2003 version are  not created by father because father  does not exist rather they are produced  when a human transmutation is attempted  the transmutation as always will fail  and rather than a person being brought  back to life a new being is created  instead a monster with their genetics  and some of their memories but still  entirely its own if this monster is fed  red stones they will become more  powerful and eventually a full-fledged  homunculus what i really like about this  is that it makes the consequences for  their actions go beyond just themselves  ed doesn't just lose an arm and a leg he  creates an actual monster in the world  the taboo of human transmutation and  alchemy is a form of social contract  there is a responsibility and promise  that comes with being an alchemist that  you will not breach this and as such it  makes sense for there to be real world  social consequences when that contract  is breached all of the homunculus in the  2003 version also share a weakness in  that if the bones of their original body  are brought nearby they are weakened and  if it's close enough they are entirely  paralyzed now i'm only going to explain  the major changes and the homunculus  origins because otherwise it would get  very repetitive so just keep that in  mind going  forward full metal alchemist  starting with lust she was created when  scar's brother attempted to bring back  his dead lover and as such he was made  in his lover's image which can i just  say  nice less personality is largely similar  between the virgins however what she  lusts for in this version is to become  human to meet this end she will lead  alchemist to seek out the philosopher's  stone hoping that she can take it and  give it to dante who would use it to  make her human however she eventually  learns that dante is lying to her and  defects ultimately leading dante to send  wrath to kill her as she dies she  wonders where homunculus will go once  they pass on while lust is still pretty  savage at times in this version the much  more human element i think goes a long  way into making her a very sympathetic  character  full metal alchemist  gluttony in the 2003 version is almost  the same as brotherhood until he learns  of lust death of course this time dante  lobotomizes him ultimately leading him  to become a pure sense of gluttony  devouring everything and everyone in his  path including eventually dante in 2003  he is also not a false gate of truth  rather he was created by dante to drink  the red water and to consume human flesh  until they condensed in his stomach and  made a new philosopher's stone however  the core themes of his character being  one that is created by father or dante  to meet their ultimate goal is still  something that is very much held intact  full metal alchemist  envy in the 2003 version was the first  homunculus created and was created when  hohenheim tried to revive he and dante's  dead son envy hated hohenheim for  abandoning both he and his mother and as  you might imagine he was a bit envious  of the elric brothers who received some  of hohenheim's affection and fatherly  love unlike the other homunculi he has  no real desire to become human instead  he just wants to kill as many people as  he can  full metal alchemist  2003 greed was created by dante and much  like his brotherhood counterpart he  eventually rebelled against his creator  he wanted a truly immortal body trying  to get edward to bind his soul to armor  just like al's had been of course there  is no greedling in this version as ling  is not a character but it is also  important to note that greed is another  character who doesn't really care about  becoming human so those are the ones  that more or less translate somewhat  directly from brotherhood to this  version the rest are completely  reimagined characters for the most part  full metal alchemist  wrath in this version was created when  izumi curtis tried to revive her  stillborn son when the resurrected  corpse was not her child she decided to  give it back to the gate but as the gate  closed in front of her she began to hear  the baby cry and regretted not keeping  it as wrath grew older he eventually  opened the gate himself but emerged with  no memories he had found himself on yok  island and eventually was taken in by  the curtis family for a short time until  the military captured him and envy took  the opportunity to feed him red stones  unlocking his true personality from here  wrath decides to join the homunculi  where he latched onto sloth as a new  adopted mother wrath in 2003 had a  powerful bloodlust after eating the red  stones very different to whom he was  prior for much of the story wrath also  had edward's missing arm and leg which  resulted in him being a homunculi who  could perform alchemy making him a very  powerful opponent  full metal alchemist  sloth is probably one of my favorite  characters in the 2003 version and maybe  even in full metal alchemist in general  which is ironic because of how much i  dislike the other version of sloth she  was created by edward when he tried to  revive his mother and as such she looks  just like her sloth in this case does  not refer to slow movement or laziness  like it does in brotherhood it instead  refers to her apathetic personality as  for her unique ability she can turn  parts of herself into flowing water that  she can kind of control at will she  plays a very interesting role in the  story as she shares some of trisha  elric's memories and is very much  disturbed by them but at the same time  she uses the memory of trisha within ed  al and hohenheim to make openings that  she can take advantage of  full metal alchemist  finally we have 2003's pride which of  course  is fewer king bradley rather than him  being wrath like he was in brotherhood  he plays very much a similar role racing  through the military to become fuhrer  and manipulating a mistress to produce a  philosopher's stone there are a few big  differences between the king bradleys  though namely this version is still able  to regenerate when injured making him  even more dangerous he even allows  mustang to blow him up and regenerates  from next to nothing furthermore this  time he is much more savage than he was  in brotherhood which says a lot because  that bradley was also kind of a monster  the only reason they were able to defeat  him in this version is because as his  house burns down salim brings him a  treasure from his locked safe he did  this in hopes of protecting what he  thought was his father's most prized  possession however the treasure was the  skull of the man he had been born from  in a fin of rage bradley strangles his  son to death and afterwards due to being  weakened by his closeness to the skull  mustang is able to take him down just as  he had with lust in brotherhood  full metal alchemist  and the last character we have to cover  is dante the big bad from the original  fullmetal alchemist dante transfers her  soul from person to person using a  philosopher's stone to prolong her life  four centuries ago she started doing the  nasty with hohenheim and they were able  to live together for centuries because  of this ability they even had a son who  unfortunately died at 18.  as mentioned previously hohenheim tries  to revive this boy and he would  eventually become envy together dante  and hohenheim would go on to destroy two  major cities as they prolong their own  life turning the inhabitants of these  cities into philosopher's stones and  jumping into new bodies  eventually hohenheim would leave dante  though and fell in love with tricia  elric now alone dante began creating  homunculi feeding the husts that  remained from human transmutation red  stones and convincing them to work for  her if they did so she promised to make  them human once she got the  philosopher's stone this was of course a  lie and instead she only wanted to  extend her own life the only homunculi  who knew the truth were pride and envy  pride went along with it because he  received a position of power while envy  just wanted to murder people ultimately  dante's immortality was far from perfect  when she jumped to her new host she  always left behind a part of her soul  becoming more and more hollow each time  she did this as a result with her final  jump in the series her soul is having  difficulty sustaining a human body this  doesn't entirely matter all that much in  the grand scheme of things though as  either way she is devoured by gluttony  and that's it a look at both versions of  fullmetal alchemists homunculi and their  leaders there are definitely good parts  of both the viciousness of brotherhood's  monkey life and the humanity in the 2003  versions personally i think i like the  2003 versions more as a whole but i  totally understand liking the other  version more to me lust wrath and sloth  in 2003 are just so much more  interesting whereas bradley and greed  are much more interesting in brotherhood  also i think father is probably a little  bit more interesting than dante although  dante not so bad herself and that kind  of only leaves envy and gluttony envy is  a total toss-up both versions are very  good for different reasons and gluttony  is just kind of gluttony so you know  doesn't super matter but i would love to  hear your own opinions in the comments  down below which version of homunculi do  you like best and which homunculus is  your favorite finally if you guys  enjoyed this fullmetal alchemist video  and you want to see more please leave a  like and if you're new to anime uproar  remember to subscribe and ring that bell  by selecting all notifications you can  guarantee that you will not miss any  future videos and of course you can also  follow anime uproar on twitter and  instagram at anime uproar or you can  follow myself at excellionyt i want to  give a big thank you to all of our anime  uproar patrons who make videos like this  one possible special thanks to alpha  sigma who is an absolute mad lad and  disciple of lord twego himself and of  course our the one tier patrons the ones  who rise above all other clans these  being ingrada patahepha al-jatal  hinokami and water the toasted chi the  spike 8227 dylan isadore spidey life  tenell tungsten tarkis baked buddhist  and monkey d quilly and finally thank  you to all of our pro hero tier patrons  the one and only gilgamesh the  red-haired raven angel cruz rathuen de  ora very gucci alicia octor bonnie parks  joanne garcia ted not ted fatboy games  corey mcgowan and soul ray slice and  dice if you enjoy our videos and feel  like they provide some kind of value to  you please consider checking out our  patreon through the link in the  description anyone who supports the  channel with even a single dollar has  access to our exclusive patreon only  discord and your name will appear at the  end of videos just like all of these  phenomenal people but for now i want to  thank you all so much for watching and  until next time remember to stay active  [Music]  you
 

